{"name":"Medusa","hex":"#559260","fetched":"2026-10-17","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Medusa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the phylum Cnidaria – diverse jellyfishes, now assigned to numerous other genera."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The youngest and only mortal of the three gorgon sisters, killed by Perseus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Medusa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Medusa","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Medusa, also called Gorgo or the Gorgon, was one of the three Gorgons. Medusa is generally described as a woman with living snakes in place of hair; her appearance was so hideous that anyone who looked upon her was turned to stone. Medusa and her Gorgon sisters Euryale and Stheno were usually described as daughters of Phorcys and Ceto; of the three, only Medusa was mortal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Gorgona_pushkin.jpg/330px-Gorgona_pushkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medusa","wikidata":"Q160730"},{"title":"Medusa (Annie Lennox album)","blocks":[{"text":"Medusa is the second solo studio album by Scottish singer Annie Lennox, released on 6 March 1995 by RCA Records. It consists entirely of cover songs. The album entered the UK Albums Chart at number one and peaked in the United States at number 11, spending 60 weeks on the Billboard 200. It has since achieved double platinum status in both the United Kingdom and the United States. As of 2018, Medusa had sold over six million copies worldwide."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d9/Annie_Lennox_-_Medusa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medusa_(Annie_Lennox_album)","wikidata":"Q617045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Gorgona_pushkin.jpg/500px-Gorgona_p